[2m│[0m [1m[38;5;231m30 of the 425 asks on disk carry a multiSelect question, where the widget wants space-to-toggle then enter. How should
[0;2m│[0m [1m[38;5;231mthe phone drive that?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mOne tap = one toggle, then a separate done (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mTapping an option sends 'step to it + space' and nothing else. The next poll re-reads the pane, which paints the [39m
     [38;5;246mtoggle state per row, so the phone renders checked options as checked from the screen rather than from local [39m
     [38;5;246mmemory. A separate 'done' button sends enter. Costs a 4s poll per toggle.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Collect locally, send one sequence
     [38;5;246mThe phone tracks which options you ticked and, on 'done', sends the whole script: step, space, step, space, enter.
[39m     [38;5;246mOne round trip and no poll latency between taps, which matters when you are ticking three of four options. But it [39m
     [38;5;246mis an intermediate state that is never re-read, so one dropped keystroke silently mis-toggles everything after it.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Send multiSelect to free text
     [38;5;246mRender the options read-only and answer through the widget's free-text row in prose. No toggle arithmetic at all, [39m
     [38;5;246mand multiSelect stops being a distinct code path. But it converts a structured answer into text the receiving [39m
     [38;5;246mClaude has to re-interpret, and 30 of 425 is frequent enough that this would be a visible downgrade rather than an
[39m     [38;5;246medge case.[39m
  [38;5;246m4. Type something.[39m
